 "content_notes": "Closed: Pablo Escobar died on 2 December 1993; there was no trial. Nothing of his death is depicted: the raid is officers at a door under police lights, the roof stays empty, and the death is one spoken summary line plus a typed card; who fired the fatal shot is a card ('still disputed'), not narration. No weapon, drug, cash, bomb, aircraft wreck, victim, body or blood is drawn anywhere; the jet bombing and the police bounties are a typed card in a quiet ops room. Escobar appears ONLY as an anonymous rim-lit silhouette (characters/figures/pe35_escobar.json; 'ILLUSTRATION · NOT A LIKENESS'), never a photo recreation, never posed heroically, none of his words quoted. His son is never drawn and is referred to only as 'his son' (he later changed his name); his account is attributed ('his son says', CNN 2016). The officers and agents are generic figures with no insignia; Col. Martínez and the convicted hitman are not named on screen. The radiotelephone is a generic 1990s brick handset with no brand; the room, street, van, house and hillside are generic drawings, not the real places. Every card is our own typed graphic; no real police, court, DEA or press material is imitated. No dialogue is invented. Facts verified 2026-10-13 from search-result extracts only.",
